    "marker_color": 6,
    "source_object": "The vertical 8-3-0 object at column 20, rows 1-3.",
    "interpretation": "Each isolated 6 is a trigger for a copy of that source object, retaining its vertical orientation. The demos indicate that marker color selects the source object; they do not justify assuming the 6 itself corresponds to a particular value in the copied object. In particular, the exact anchor/alignment should follow the placement convention demonstrated for this source-object type, not be guessed from the marker’s color."
